A||||9||Formula||will 215-70-15s fit on a formla/GT?||||1||
Z||000000||Formula||06-11-2000||09:29 AM||||will 215-70-15 tires fit on a formula or GT?||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||06-11-2000||10:03 AM||||No problem as long as it's not lowered.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Terrybogin||06-11-2000||10:30 AM||||They should work as long as they are not white walls on wire basket wheels. Then you would be laughed off the Forum  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT Bastard||06-11-2000||12:08 PM||||70's seem kinda tall though.... It might look strange.  Did someone give you a good deal on some 70's?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||06-11-2000||01:38 PM||||They'll work but handling will suffer and your speedometer will be 10% off. So if you are driving at 60mph you will really be going 66mph. The tire you chose is 2" taller than the stock tires. It may rub a little with the steering fully turned. The sidewall is 6" so in a hard corner the tire will roll onto the sidewall more than a stock. With the 2" taller sidewalls it will fill up the wheel well better.||||reg||13
Z||000005||phillip||06-11-2000||04:55 PM||||try this <BR>215-70/15<BR>a=215 <BR>b=70<BR>c=15<BR>a X .03937=how wide tire is in inches<BR>width X b(.70) X 2 + 15= height of wheel/tire combo        <BR> <BR>it's not exact since all tires aren't exactly the same from the various manufacturers, but it's good for approximating. i use this all the time.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula||06-12-2000||09:00 AM||||I got a really good deal on them but I think I'll pass on them.  btw... they arent white walls. lol||||reg||1
Z||000007||lennyb4||06-12-2000||10:20 AM||||Im currently running BFG 215/70/14's all the way around. I really havent noticed that much of a difference in handling (unless i try a really sharp turn, then she leans alittle). I got them for two reasons. 1st: i got a great deal on them. 2nd: i like the way they fill the fender well up. BUT if you do go with them i have noticed some light scrubbing on the front if im turning and hit a decent bump (esp. coming out of my driveway).<P>[This message has been edited by lennyb4 (edited 06-12-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by lennyb4 (edited 06-12-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000008||Formula||06-12-2000||10:51 PM||||I ended up getting 225/60-15s on the back and 205/60-15s on the front....<P>and I also did a comple brake job (rotors,calipers, lines etc.....)....<P>and I still have the new struts and shocks!<P>It better handle, stop, and ride like a new fiero.  lol, now i just need ACCELERATION!||||reg||1
Z||000009||Eric||06-12-2000||11:57 PM||||Keep me posted on how those rear tires wear.  My 88GT likes to eat up that size tire on a stock rim.  It wears from the middle out.  The middle is almost bald after 5k miles and it's not from doing burnouts or having my pressure too high either.  I also have -2 degrees of camber in the rear and the inside still has the knobbies from the molding.||||reg||1
